WEBVTT

NOTE Scene 04A. Speaker labels and dialogue derive from the original script.
NOTE Time positions aligned using faster-whisper word timestamps; human review still required.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
<v Jack Marlowe>Sterling's office occupied the top floor of a building that looked down on everybody,

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:09.780
<v Jack Marlowe>which was probably why he liked it. I waited until Betty called to confirm the

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.420
<v Jack Marlowe>ledger was safe with the attorney.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.200
<v Victor Sterling>Mr. Marlow. Do you have an appointment?

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.580
<v Jack Marlowe>No, but I've got a copy of a ledger.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.100
<v Victor Sterling>I beg your pardon?

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.680
<v Jack Marlowe>That's usually what happens before the sentencing.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.740
<v Victor Sterling>I don't know what you're implying.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.500
<v Jack Marlowe>I'm implying that a lot of people paid their insurance premiums and you bought

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.820
<v Jack Marlowe>yourself a very expensive fireplace.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.780
<v Victor Sterling>My companies have experienced certain unfortunate financial difficulties.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.060
<v Jack Marlowe>Sure. Their money had difficulty staying out of your pocket.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.280
<v Victor Sterling>What do you want?

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.080
<v Jack Marlowe>The truth about Ernest Cross.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.280
<v Victor Sterling>A tragic disappearance. A fine man.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.380
<v Jack Marlowe>So fine you sent Knuckles after his hat.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.380
<v Victor Sterling>You have no proof of that.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.860
<v Jack Marlowe>I've got a copy of the accounts and a very interesting letter.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.080
<v Jack Marlowe>By tomorrow morning, every newspaper in town could have a copy.

00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:05.380
<v Victor Sterling>Five thousand dollars. For your silence.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:06.960
<v Jack Marlowe>Tempting.

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:08.626
<v Victor Sterling>Ten thousand.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.680
<v Jack Marlowe>You're making it difficult to be an upstanding citizen.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.120
<v Victor Sterling>Knuckles! Get in here!

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.620
<v Knuckles Malone>Hey, boss. Ya wanted me?

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:18.440
<v Victor Sterling>Remove this man!

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.120
<v Knuckles Malone>What, from the office?

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.260
<v Victor Sterling>YES!

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.700
<v Knuckles Malone>Permanently, or just, ya know, downstairs?

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.500
<v Jack Marlowe>Think carefully. The district attorney already knows about the ledger.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.600
<v Jack Marlowe>I'd hate to see you get arrested for your employer's bad bookkeeping.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.920
<v Knuckles Malone>The district attorney? Boss, ya said this was a legitimate business!

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.540
<v Victor Sterling>Of course I took the money! Cross was going to ruin everything!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.000
<v Victor Sterling>I told you to retrieve the evidence, not advertise the entire operation!

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:49.840
<v Knuckles Malone>I ain't much good at advertising, boss.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.640
<v Jack Marlowe>That's quite a confession. Betty, did you get all that?

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.620
<v Betty>Every word, boss! The attorney's right here with me.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.100
<v Betty>Nice loud telephone ya got there, Mr. Sterling!

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.740
<v Victor Sterling>You left the receiver off the hook?

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.040
<v Jack Marlowe>I was worried about the long-distance charges.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.760
<v Victor Sterling>Very well. Have your attorney contact mine.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:11.620
<v Victor Sterling>I'll cooperate.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.080
<v Knuckles Malone>Does that mean I get the afternoon off?

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.060
<v Jack Marlowe>Sterling's attorney arranged his surrender to the authorities.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:23.180
<v Jack Marlowe>Betty had a witness to his confession, and Knuckles suddenly remembered a great

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:28.380
<v Jack Marlowe>many things about his employer. I left the building considerably happier than

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.600
<v Jack Marlowe>the man on the top floor.

